# Git Commits

- ALWAYS use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/): `<type>(<optional scope>): <subject>`
  - Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`
  - Scopes (optional): `cli`, `detect`, `registry`, `plan`, `targets`, `io`, `ui`, `docs`, `deps`, `ci`, `release`
  - Subject: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period, ≤ 72 characters
  - Breaking changes: add `!` after the type/scope and a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- Body is optional; use it to explain *why*, wrapped at 72 characters.
- NEVER add `Co-authored-by:` trailers or any AI/tool attribution (e.g. "Generated with…", "Made with…") to commit messages.
- One logical change per commit.

```text
# ✅ Good
feat(detect): resolve installed package versions from node_modules
fix(targets): serialize cursor globs as comma-separated string

# ❌ Bad
Added detection stuff.
feat: add detector

Co-authored-by: Some Agent <agent@example.com>
```
